"text": "The live smoke is the harness lifecycle (boot/status/cleanup), because the recorder touches `home.rs`'s readiness. - **Browser leg:** runs locally on the host's Node (v24.13.1, which satisfies `engines >=20`), after a host Chromium install   entry. - **WSL leg:** proven by the pre-push entry. Two plan entries run before it (overseer review direction, 2026-09-27; no operator   step): the re-provision, as the distro user under `env -i`, then the root `--install-deps` through `wsl.exe -d Ubuntu -u root`.   The installed package list is recorded in `evidence/wsl-chromium-deps.md`. - **Pinned Node download:** proven by CI's own run on each OS, because the host keeps its own Node. - **No headful self-verify gate:** none exists yet, because `viola ui` and its page arrive in Epoch 8, and the stub is a test   fixture, not a UI surface. - **One-shot control:** the recorder's remove-the-guard pair (step 13) MUTATES source and reverts, so it runs once at implement,   with both readings in `evidence/root-watch-recorder.md`. The non-mutating entries that guard it on every re-run are the   `from_secs(10)` census and the `zz_root_watch_control` census. - **`npx --no`:** every `npx` form carries `--no`, so a missing local package fails instead of fetching the registry's newest   Playwright."
}
